Report the real release version in MSLK_PYTHON_ONLY builds

The python-only branch of setup.py hardcodes version 0.0.0 (that is what the
PyPI name-reservation wheel carries).  Building the GitHub archive with
MSLK_PYTHON_ONLY=1 would therefore install a package that reports
0.0.0 through mslk.__version__ and importlib.metadata.  Read the version from
the environment instead, keeping the upstream default when it is unset.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -587,7 +587,10 @@
     if _PYTHON_ONLY:
         print("[SETUP.PY] MSLK_PYTHON_ONLY=1 — skipping C++/CUDA build")
         package_name = "mslk"
-        package_version = "0.0.0"
+        # Gentoo: this is a GitHub archive without git metadata and the
+        # package version is not derived from it here, so let the ebuild
+        # tell us which release we are installing.  Upstream default kept.
+        package_version = os.environ.get("MSLK_VERSION", "0.0.0")
         _write_version_file(package_version, "default", "python_only")
 
     else:
